e>Myers</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Health status among farm workers in the Western Cape&#x02013;collateral evidence from a study of occupational hazards</article-title><source>S Afr Med J</source><year>1998</year><volume>88</volume><fpage>1096</fpage><lpage>1101</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">London L, Nell V, Thompson ML, Myers JF (1998) Health status among farm workers in the Western Cape&#x02013;collateral evidence from a study of occupational hazards. S Afr Med J 88:1096&#x02013;1101 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9798496</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lu</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Risk factors to pesticide exposure and associated health symptoms among cut-flower farmers</article-title><source>Int J Environ Health Res</source><year>2005</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>161</fpage><lpage>169</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1080/09603120500105638</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Lu JL (2005) Risk factors to pesticide exposure and associated health symptoms among cut-flower farmers. Int J Environ Health Res 15:161&#x02013;169. doi:10.1080/09603120500105638 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16134479</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mancini</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Bruggen</surname><given-names>AH</given-names></name><name><surname>Jiggins</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Ambatipudi</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Murphy</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Acute pesticide poisoning among female and male cotton growers in India</article-title><source>Int J Occup Environ Health</source><year>2005</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>221</fpage><lpage>232</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Mancini F, Van Bruggen AH, Jiggins JL, Ambatipudi AC, Murphy H (2005) Acute pesticide poisoning among female and male cotton growers in India. Int J Occup Environ Health 11:221&#x02013;232 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16130962</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Matthews</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Operator exposure to pesticides</article-title><source>Pestic Outlook</source><year>2002</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>233</fpage><lpage>237</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1039/b211168n</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Matthews GA (2002) Operator exposure to pesticides. Pestic Outlook 13:233&#x02013;237. doi:10.1039/b211168n </citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Matthews</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Attitudes and behaviours regarding use of crop protection products&#x02014;A survey of more than 8500 smallholders in 26 countries</article-title><source>Crop Prot</source><year>2008</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>834</fpage><lpage>846</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.cropro.2007.10.013</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Matthews GA (2008) Attitudes and behaviours regarding use of crop protection products&#x02014;A survey of more than 8500 smallholders in 26 countries. Crop Prot 27:834&#x02013;846. doi:10.1016/j.cropro.2007.10.013 </citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ngowi</surname><given-names>AV</given-names></name><name><surname>Maeda</surname><given-names>DN</given-names></name><name><surname>Partanen</surname><given-names>TJ</give